## §3 Slot lifecycle

`POD_combat_slot` story type (declared in `POD_story_cycle_combat.txt`)
is the sole data container for per-combatant state. Lifecycle helpers
live in `pod_combat_slot_effects.txt`:

- `pod_combat_create_slot_stories_effect` runs once at combat start
  from `pod_combat_initialize_effect`, BEFORE any per-slot init runs
  (so `pod_combat_init_slot_from_character_effect` can read/write
  the slot story for the slot it's populating).
- `pod_combat_clear_slot_stories_effect` runs once at combat end
  from `pod_combat_group_cleanup_effect`. `end_story` takes every
  slot var with it, so no per-field cleanup pass is needed.

**Caller scope:** the combat host (the PC). All saves / list adds
happen on the host; the actual stories live on Charon
(`POD_wraith_01`) like the move catalogue and log entries.

### Walking slots: list iteration vs unrolled 0..9

There are two slot-walking lists and one unrolled-call pattern in
this codebase. They are NOT interchangeable — picking the wrong one
leads to either spurious work, missed slots, or stale-story leaks.
The rule:

- **`every_in_list = { variable = pod_combat_active_slots ... }`** —
  the default for nearly every "operate on slots" pass. Filled-only
  (populated by `pod_combat_set_slot_char_effect` at fill time,
  cleared at combat end). KO'd-but-once-filled slots stay in the
  list with `slot_alive = 0`, so add `var:slot_alive = 1` to the
  limit if you only want active combatants. Examples: round-end
  soak revert, victory-check team counts, dispatching to the slot
  whose `slot_index = pod_combat_current_actor`, AoE damage / heal
  / buff / debuff iteration, post-combat duel teardown, post-combat
  nonfatal wound cap, tier var cleanup. Inside the body the
  iterator's scope IS the slot story, so `var:slot_X` reads and
  `set_variable = { name = slot_X ... }` writes work directly. To
  reach back to host vars, save the host first (`save_scope_as = host`
  or `save_temporary_scope_as = host` for trigger contexts) and
  reference `scope:host.var:Y`.

- **`every_in_list = { variable = pod_combat_slots ... }`** —
  reserved for combat-end teardown. Contains all 10 created slot
  stories regardless of fill. The only legitimate use is
  `pod_combat_clear_slot_stories_effect`'s `end_story` walk, which
  must end every story (filled or not) to prevent leaking unfilled
  stories on Charon. Do NOT pick this list for any other walk —
  it forces a `has_variable = slot_char` filter that
  `pod_combat_active_slots` makes redundant, and walks 10 stories
  when typically only 2–6 are filled.

- **Unrolled `SLOT = 0..9` parametric calls** — ONLY for the slot
  creation / fill passes that run BEFORE `pod_combat_active_slots`
  has been populated, or for single-slot operations where a specific
  slot index is intentional (slot 0 = PC, slot 5 = primary opponent).
  The init walks in `pod_combat_initialize_effect` are the canonical
  examples; the per-team hit-chance pair-up walk is another (slot N
  vs leader, where N is enumerated).

The `any_in_list` trigger is the read-only counterpart over
`pod_combat_active_slots`: use it for "does any slot satisfy X?"
questions in trigger context (e.g. "is the targeting requirement
satisfied — does any alive enemy exist?"). Pre-Phase-3 the codebase
carried unrolled OR chains for these; the consolidation pass
replaced them with `any_in_list` predicates.

### Slot creation field defaults

`pod_combat_create_one_slot_story_effect` initializes each slot
story with:

| Field | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `slot_index` | the slot's integer position (0-9) | baked at creation |
| `slot_alive` | 1 | the slot is "occupied" until KO'd; init effect for individual fields will overwrite if the slot is unfilled |
| `slot_morale` | 0 | overwritten from character if filled |
| `slot_prowess` | 0 | same |
| `slot_soak` | 0 | same |
| `slot_energy_used` | 0 | same |
| `slot_has_acted` | 0 | same |

These fields are pure values (no absence-as-signal semantics) so a
default of 0 is safe — readers gate on `has_variable =
pod_combat_slot_$SLOT$` (the slot exists) and just read the value.

### Fields NOT pre-initialized (deliberately absence-as-signal)

| Field | Absence semantics |
|---|---|
| `slot_char` | meaningful only as a scope reference; absence = "slot is empty" |
| `slot_base_soak` | gate for the round-end soak revert in `pod_combat_clear_per_turn_slot_state_effect` (filters the `pod_combat_active_slots` walk that resets `slot_soak` to its base) |
| `slot_hit_chance` | gate for the synthesis fallback in `pod_combat_slot_hit_chance_value` (the fallback fires when `hit_chance` hasn't been written yet by `calculate_all_hit_chances`) |
| `slot_base_hit_chance` | gate in `pod_combat_recalc_slot_stats_effect` |
| `slot_initiative` | set during initiative calc (alive slots only); presence distinguishes "filled-and-rolled this round" from "unfilled or pre-calc" |
| `slot_turn_order` | turn rank within the round, stamped by `pod_combat_calc_turn_orders_effect` after initiative is rolled |
| `slot_init_bonus` | presence = active initiative bonus to fold into the next initiative roll |
| `slot_ap_drain` | presence = pending AP drain to apply on the actor's next turn |
| `slot_incorporeal_spirit` | presence = combatant is incorporeal; physical attacks no-op unless the attacker has `slot_can_damage_spirit` |
| `slot_can_damage_spirit` | presence = combatant can damage incorporeal targets |
| `slot_is_guarding` / `_is_dodging` / `_is_stealthed` | stance flags |
| `slot_retaliate_*` | retaliate state |
| `slot_*_tier` | tier vars; `has_variable` detects "no buff active" |

Readers of these fields use per-field `has_variable` checks.

